# `go build ./cmd/<name>` writes its output into the working directory,
# so a plain build of any command in this repo leaves a binary at the
# root. One of them (kontur-agent) reached a commit that way; these
# entries are so the next one cannot.
/kontur
/kontur-agent
/kontur-mem-agent
/konturctl
/granule
/granule-shim
/granule-agent
/granule-mem-agent

# Everything demo/demo.sh makes on the machine it runs on: the CLI it
# builds, the VM state directory it points granule at, and the scratch
# files its steps write. One directory so that `demo/demo.sh cleanup` is
# a removal rather than a hunt.
/.demo/

# Python cache files
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The directory `granule granulefile build` stages its generated files
# in, inside the author's own build context. It removes it when the
# build ends, so one of these on disk is a build that was interrupted --
# and one in a commit is a run of test/granulefiles/run.sh that a `git
# add -A` happened to catch mid-build.
.granule-build-*/
